Finally the RNG assigned me a human rogue that I managed to *not* kill;
my very first human rogue at NAO that survived. He had the advantage
to be equipped with 14(?) daggers at start, and that helped a lot. But
beyond that the game was a bit stingy. During the difficult phases he
had no scrolls to enchant armour and not enough to enchant weapons.
He also couldn't get an artifact weapon because there was not a single
altar (besides the guaranteed temples), and mine-town altar was not
co-aligned. Lacking powerful enough pets for the dirty task, I decided
to convert the temple, but didn't want to kill the priest, so my rogue
cornered him behind a wall of boulders; where he got released later by
some troll with a wand of striking. The angry priest starts wandering
around and was after me, but I managed to lock him in one of the huts
in mine-town. In the meantime I had Orcrist and Firebrand. At that stage
I was confident that I don't need to buff my character too much with AC,
and I ate a lot wraiths from the many morgues the game had. Intrinsic
AC was thus very low during large parts of the game; AC:-13, or -10
when two-weaponing (+3 Firebrand with +0 silver sabre). Only 2 points
of divine AC; later I carried some x*10k zorkmid from Gehennom to the
Valley priest to enhance that to 4 more AC points. All ?oEW went to my
stack of 36(?) +5 daggers. The AC of -13 could only be established by
some yellow dragon and a random scroll of EA. Shortly after I used a
(Castle wand?) wish for a GDSM. My rogue was killing everything with
what he had; ranged daggers, two-weaponing with an artifact, and the
spell of magic missile at XL:28. So the late game was quite uneventful
in this respect. Without ever finding scrolls of magic mapping the
search for Vlad's entry was boring, and I had to completely map all
possible levels the hard way; the stairs were on the last examined
level in the last area I looked. An Archon at the Plane of Fire made
me anxious; not long ago I got killed by the effects of the presence
of such a beast on the Plane of Air. This time I blindfolded me in
time and teleported him away sufficiently far so that I could run and
reach the portal. Pestilence guarded the closest altar, which turned
out to be lawful. Rethinking about his dirty deeds the rogue reformed,
converted from chaotic to lawful and left the place in the usual chaos.

